// The base the packages IN THIS REPO extend — and it extends the one abide ships to apps, so there
// is one statement of what a `.abide` program is and the two apps here read it through the same
// public specifier an app outside this repo would.
//
// What used to be here and is gone is the PROGRAM: one `include` covering every package, and one
// `paths` map answering for all of them. That map is why `$server` / `$ui` / `$shared` could only
// ever mean `packages/abide`'s seams — `paths` is program-global, so a second package meaning its own
// by those names was not a rule anybody was keeping, it was an impossibility. Each package now owns
// its own config, `abide check` runs the checker per package, and the seams are `package.json`
// subpath imports — `#shared`, `#ui`, `#server` — which are scoped to the package the importing FILE
// is in, and which Bun, `tsc` and `Bun.build` all resolve without being told.
//
// `files: []` and no `include`, so this file is a base and never a program of its own — a bare `tsc`
// here checks nothing rather than assembling every package into the one program that was the problem.
{
    "extends": "./packages/abide/app.tsconfig.json",
    "files": []
}
